# Helion Particle Lab environment variables
#
# The app runs with ZERO env vars locally: it falls back to an embedded
# PGLite (Postgres-in-WASM) database that needs no configuration. Copy this
# file to `.env` only when you want to point at a real database or turn on
# authentication for a hosted deploy.

# DATABASE_URL (optional locally, RECOMMENDED for deploys)
# Postgres connection string. When set, the app (src/lib/db.ts) and the
# build-time migrator (scripts/migrate.mjs) use hosted Postgres instead of
# the embedded PGLite fallback. Any pg-compatible provider works; a free
# Neon database is the easiest to create from a phone.
# IMPORTANT: without DATABASE_URL the app still runs, but PGLite storage is
# in-memory and does NOT persist across serverless invocations, so any data
# is lost between requests on a hosted deploy. Set this for real persistence.
# DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:password@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (OPTIONAL and non-blocking)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The particle simulator AND the feedback system run fully WITHOUT signing in.
# Auth is optional: nothing below is required to run or deploy the app, and no
# one is ever forced to sign in.
#
# Sign-in is REAL, self-hosted Better Auth (src/lib/auth/server.ts) at
# same-origin /api/auth/* against YOUR OWN database — no external broker.
#   - Email + password: works with ZERO extra config locally (embedded PGLite).
#   - Google OAuth: OPTIONAL; only turns on when BOTH GOOGLE_CLIENT_* are set.
#
# For a PERSISTENT hosted deploy (Vercel), set these three:
#   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, BETTER_AUTH_URL, and DATABASE_URL (above).
# Email/password sign-in needs nothing more than those.

# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET (REQUIRED for a hosted deploy)
#   Signs auth sessions. Locally a process-stable secret is generated for you,
#   but a deploy MUST set a stable value or sessions break across restarts /
#   instances. Generate your own with:
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#   Do NOT reuse the placeholder below; paste your own generated secret.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-output-of-openssl-rand-hex-32"

# BETTER_AUTH_URL (REQUIRED for a hosted deploy)
#   The public base URL of your deployment. Better Auth uses it as its base URL
#   and trusted origin. On Vercel this is your project URL, e.g.
#     https://built-helion.vercel.app
#   Locally the app defaults to http://localhost:3000, so you can leave it unset
#   for `npm run dev`.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL="https://built-helion.vercel.app"

# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET (OPTIONAL — enables Google sign-in)
#   Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID in the Google Cloud Console
#   (https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials) and set BOTH values.
#   Add this Authorized redirect URI (Better Auth's Google callback path),
#   replacing the host with your BETTER_AUTH_URL:
#     https://built-helion.vercel.app/api/auth/callback/google
#   Supplying only one of the two leaves Google OFF. Its absence never affects
#   email/password or the rest of the app.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="your-google-oauth-client-id"
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET="your-google-oauth-client-secret"

# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID / GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET (OPTIONAL — enables GitHub sign-in)
#   GitHub OAuth is FREE. Register an OAuth App at
#   https://github.com/settings/developers ("New OAuth App") and set BOTH values.
#   Set the Authorization callback URL (Better Auth's GitHub callback path),
#   replacing the host with your BETTER_AUTH_URL:
#     https://built-helion.vercel.app/api/auth/callback/github
#   Supplying only one of the two leaves GitHub OFF. Its absence never affects
#   email/password or the rest of the app.
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID="your-github-oauth-client-id"
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET="your-github-oauth-client-secret"

# Sign in with Apple (OPTIONAL — enables Apple sign-in)
#   Apple sign-in requires a PAID Apple Developer account ($99/yr) and stays
#   OFF until ALL FOUR of the values below are set (any one missing = Apple is
#   hidden, no code change needed to turn it on later).
#
#   Unlike Google/GitHub there is NO static client secret to paste: Apple's
#   OAuth client secret is a short-lived ES256 JWT the app GENERATES for you
#   (src/lib/auth/apple-secret.server.ts) from the four values below. You supply
#   the raw ingredients, not a secret.
#
#   To obtain these in the Apple Developer portal (https://developer.apple.com):
#     1. Register an App ID with "Sign in with Apple" enabled.
#     2. Create a Services ID — its identifier is APPLE_CLIENT_ID below. Enable
#        "Sign in with Apple" on it and add this Return URL / callback,
#        replacing the host with your BETTER_AUTH_URL:
#          https://built-helion.vercel.app/api/auth/callback/apple
#     3. Create a Sign in with Apple KEY, download the .p8 file once — its
#        contents are APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY and its Key ID is APPLE_KEY_ID.
#     4. APPLE_TEAM_ID is your 10-character Apple Developer Team ID.
#
#   APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY is the FULL .p8 contents (the multi-line PEM). In a Vercel
#   env var it is fine to store it with literal "\n" between lines — the app
#   normalizes those to real newlines before signing.
#
#   APPLE_APP_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER is OPTIONAL and only needed for a NATIVE iOS/
#   macOS app that authenticates with Apple directly (not required for web).
# APPLE_CLIENT_ID="com.yourcompany.yourapp.service"
# APPLE_TEAM_ID="your-10-char-team-id"
# APPLE_KEY_ID="your-apple-key-id"
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...your .p8 contents...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"
# APPLE_APP_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER="com.yourcompany.yourapp"

# VITE_AUTH_ENABLED (OPTIONAL off-switch)
#   Read only as an OFF switch: `env("VITE_AUTH_ENABLED") === "false"`. Set it
#   to "false" to force auth off everywhere (the app uses a local dev user and
#   hides sign-in UI). Leaving it unset behaves like enabled.
# VITE_AUTH_ENABLED="false"
